Z||000013||Fformula88||11-05-2001||10:14 AM||||Del Sol's have conservative styling which turns some people off, but I really like them.  How many targa top two seaters could you have bought in its price range?  The Miata was really its only competition, and if you got the VTEC del Sol, you could spank Miatas all day long.<P>Also, about the power... Maybe you drove an S version.  del Sol's came in 3 flavors: economy S, mid-grade SI and the 160 HP VTEC versions.  I do not know the exact numbers, but the S was right around 100 HP and very much a dog.  The SI's, although not all that fast weren't bad either.  With a stick they were liveable.  The VTEC's were fairly fast.  Not V8 fast or anything, but I bet they would give a Fiero GT a good fight anyway.  Those things are light!<P>Its too bad they scrapped it instead of trying to liven up its design a little.  With sportier styling, and Acura's RSX Type-S 200 hp engine, I bet it would have been a lot of fun!  But please, no 50 HP stickers!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000014||TRiAD||11-05-2001||11:16 AM||||S=106 hp, Si=127HP SOHC VTEC, VTEC=160HP DOHC VTEC. <P>I had a del Sol Si for about a year. Excellenty car, except the FWD. VERY quick. (I had it down to 0-60 in about 6.8 with few mods)<P>Honda did make a MR turbo car (like the one in GT1) for LM. The del Sol was originally designed as a MR car, and even in production had a serious rear firewall. <P>Ah, if it were MR I'd still have one...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAlAL0S2vLvViYU9P7uloj72fLFTqfz59trng8I7AOG7hGCvfk6WP96n!gnOaEUAvooy1kUoWucv7BJ7L5EWg/temp-sig.gif">     <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 11-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Nashco||11-05-2001||11:50 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Smoooooth GT:<BR><B> Bryce...  Sound's like your drinking tonight and REALLY TRYING TO START A FLAME WAR!!! Calm down buddy!!!  Why are you sooo defensive of Honda's??  Steve</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Drinking?  I don't drink..never have/will.  I'm by no means trying to start a flame war, I didn't start the thread.  I get bothered that people slam Hondas all the time, without knowing the whole story.  See, 160 hp stock!  How many horse did the GT have at best?  How heavy is the Del Sol?  Think about those things before you assure yourself that a stock GT is quicker than it...<P>Also, who says Honda doesn't do something right 99% of the time?  Honda has outstanding quality, reliability, performance, and customer service in every aspect of their business, not just automobiles.  I wish that the American car companies would learn a lesson, and employees would take note of these things.  We wouldn't have to worry about the "Japanese Invasion" of the automotive market in the last 10 years if our quality and price could beat theirs.  It gets on my nerves that people down Hondas, usually because of the guys with stock civics plastered with stickers.  The sticker isn't Honda, the economy car underneath the sticker is.<P>Just a little anti-slam venting.  I guess I am "sooo defensive" about Honda's because I like them.<P>Oh, I agree with firstfiero, Gran Tourismo is amazingly realistic...especially 3!<P>Also, Fformula88 brings up a good point, how many targa two seaters could you buy in that range?  Maybe an old 914 or X1/9, but what kind of performance and quality would you get in comparison?  Miatas are a close one, but with the 160 hp motor, you're fine.<P>If they offered a 200 hp version, like the RSX, I'd be all over that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>&lt;/RANT&gt;&lt;/VENT&gt;&lt;SIMMA DOWN NOW&gt;K&lt;/SIMMA DOWN NOW&gt;<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 11-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||WampusCat||11-05-2001||12:08 PM||||I'd take a miata over any del sol.  Rear wheel drive, great suspension, 50/50 weight distribution, and in my opinion, MUCH better looking.  I'm seeing early models for sale for around $4,000 now.  The fieros are still a better deal (my 60k mile car was $2800) but those miatas handle really nicely and there is tons of aftermarket performance stuff out there. <A HREF="http://www.miata.net/marketplace.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.miata.net/marketplace.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||falconhulk||11-05-2001||02:09 PM||||WampusCat<BR>I agree entirely. Looking for a 90 or 91 miata right now.  Alot of them have after market turbos and superchargers on them.  Apparently the miata community is like the fiero community.  They are cool little cars||||reg||1
