Z||000019||MinnGreenGT||11-05-2001||02:26 PM||||Guys... we already did the Del Sol thing!  Read this link: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011108.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011108.html</A> <P>BTW: Gran Toursimo is cool, but I have a 650hp DelSol in GT2... that's too much power to handle correctly in that small of a car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||MinnGreenGT||11-05-2001||02:30 PM||||Hehe... I think triad posted this in the other thread  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0RgCuGo0Wpe0dBZVWLNqJ!OgcQq654Mh9B*P3DsSLyL7Jq1249HX4l55pKsdufTAOkoEwUubBTWNxu*SB72sRf5PSpElv!BVmIMZ6T1CP4!A/del-Sol-TSC-rear-2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||delSol97||11-05-2001||03:47 PM||||Having owned:<P>85 2M4<BR>85 GT<BR>90 Miata<BR>91 Miata<BR>97 delSolSi<P><BR>I can tell you that the Si will whoop a 2M4 like nothing.  It will probably even give a GT a run for its money.  Even an S is probably quicker than a 2M4.<P>A DOHC VTEC will beat a stock GT.<P>Gas mileage is not great, but its slightly better than the 2M4.<P><BR>I also road-race a Swift GTi.  Let me tell you, you can spin a FWD car around like a top.  If you can't, you just aren't driving hard enough.<P>I do dislike the wheel-hop from a FWD car though.  <P>If you are going to race a FWD car, investing in an LSD is the only way to go.<P><BR>For reference, in Speedvision Touring Car championships last year, the 2 delSol's were beating all 3 Miata's in every event.<P>A delSol VTEC will cream a Miata.<P>My delSol Si is noticably quicker than the Miata's as well.  I have not driven a 1.8L Miata though.<P>Miata's are very primitive compared to a delSol.  Ride quality/interior.  Etc.<P>I've been wanting to buy a new Miata, but I want to wait a year or two more and see what the other manufacturers come up with.<P>Maybe we'll get that MR2 Spyder in Canada some day.<P>Oh by the way, I may be adding another Fiero to my stable soon so thats why I'm here. :P<P>I like Fiero's so don't get me wrong.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||Raydar||11-05-2001||03:50 PM||||I'm glad that Rob posted that link. Beat me to it.<BR>I think DXRDAD's 300 HP Delsol would give many (most) of our cars a real kick in the shorts.<P>I'm with Bryce on this one.<BR>Honda has some <I>very good</I> engineering. AFAIK, they were the first mainstream Asian car maker to use variable valve timing. I think Infiniti <I>may</I> have beat them to it. On the Q-45. For what? $32 grand? Yeesh.<BR>Toyota is playing "catch-up", now.<P>People like to trash-talk Civics. They're a freaking <I>economy</I> car. They do what they were designed to do, and they do it well.<P>Ever driven a more expensive Honda? Accords have all sorts of neat stuff engineered in.<BR>Ever driven a 3.2 TL? <BR>Incredibly nice car. And still affordable. (Less so for some of us, than others.)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>Just my $.02.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 11-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||Slammed Fiero||11-05-2001||04:12 PM||||Perhaps in a straight line a Del sol will cream a miata , But as many many Autocrosses have shown me it's hard to beat a miata suspensionn wise.<P>They just don't have the HP.<P>FWD sports car.. there's just no such thing.<P>A friend of mine owns a honda dealership , he said Del Sol's are troublesome cars , leaky roofs and an asortment of other problems.<P>grated it nice to see someone do up something other than a Civic.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000024||TRiAD||11-05-2001||04:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Perhaps in a straight line a Del sol will cream a miata , But as many many Autocrosses have shown me it's hard to beat a miata suspensionn wise.<P>They just don't have the HP.<P>FWD sports car.. there's just no such thing.<P>A friend of mine owns a honda dealership , he said Del Sol's are troublesome cars , leaky roofs and an asortment of other problems.<P>grated it nice to see someone do up something other than a Civic.<P>JM </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have seen MANY del Sols beat their share of Miatas at the autocross...<P>I agree with the FWD thing, that's why I'm getting a Fiero.<P>Last Honda dealership I was in, the owner wouldn't know an Insight from an Echo.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Mine was VERY poorly maintained when I got it, and I never had ANY problems with it, leaks or otherwise. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000025||delSol97||11-05-2001||04:30 PM||||"Sports car" is such a stupid term anyways.<P>I see Z28's that do nothing more than go to the grocery store.<P>My goofy lookin' rollcaged Suzuki Swift GTi bangs fenders on real race tracks.<P>What is a sports car?<P><BR>Any car thats used for sport is a sports car in my opinion.<P>Of course, the real dictionary definition is a 2 seater convertible.  Which would make the Geo Metro convertible a sportscar and a Fiero GT not.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR>Same driver, a stock delSol VTEC will beat a stock Miata on a racetrack.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000026||WampusCat||11-05-2001||05:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by delSol97:<BR>[BSame driver, a stock delSol VTEC will beat a stock Miata on a racetrack.<BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Gee, I guess that's why the SCCA groups stock Miata's in B stock along with the MR2 Spyder, supercharged MR2, BMW Z3, and Porsche 914 2.0.<BR>The Del Sol VTEC is E stock along with the Mazda 626(4 cyl), 4 cyl Fiero, Hyundai Tiburon, Suzuki Swift, and Saturn 16V.<BR>Oh, and at the 2001 Solo II nationals, Miatas placed 18 of the top 25 in B stock.  There were no Del Slos in the top 25 in E stock.||||reg||1
Z||000027||Slammed Fiero||11-05-2001||05:54 PM||||THANK YOU WampusCat<P>Del Sol's don't handle as well as miatas.. This is getting off topic a bit. But I have yet too see a Del sol beat a Miata at a Divisional event.<P>The owner of the honda dealership Knows his stuff, and I believe him when he says there troublesome.<P>Z28 is a pony car.. Ever had one on a track? we rented one (a Convert automatic) and had it on the local track..Scary car..Nose dive brake fade..giddy up.<P>More at home going straight.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000028||TRiAD||11-05-2001||06:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>The owner of the honda dealership Knows his stuff, and I believe him when he says there troublesome...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah? How many has HE owned?<BR>Mine never had any of these "leak" problems, etc.<BR>There were several RUMORS about these cars (much like the Fiero "death-trap-fire-bomb"). They said the tops leaked (I've YET to tun across a del Sol owner who personally experienced this), they said the rear window would shatter if you autoXed them on race tires, due to the "chassis flex" (I raced mine, no window problems, also the del Sol had a 30% stiffer chassis than any other 5th gen Civic, call it overcompensation).<P>I would think people driving <B>Fieros</B> of all things would know better than to buy into "automotive urban legend". <BR>I guess I'm stupid. Either that, or you're just ignorant.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><I>yeah, THAT'S it...</I>||||reg||1
Z||000029||BlackDragon||11-06-2001||01:22 AM||||ok, i didn't mean to start a flame war or anything, so please dont let it turn into one.<BR>nashco: good points. there is nothing wrong with honda, its the stupid a$$es that put all the stickers on them that give them a bad name. however, I do not beleive that honda has a car worth calling fast. (note that this is MY opinion) i think honda should only be used as an economy car. there is no replacement for displacement.<P>sportscar. this is my veiw. more than two seats....NOT a sports car. under any circumstances. as far as i am concerned you can take a lamborghini and throw in a back seat and it automaticaly becomes a family car. once again, this is MY opinion.<P>i like the del sol, i think it looks good. i personaly do not like front wheel drive, though aparently it has its benifits (i am yet to descover them, but thats what i hear) i would own a del sol if i had the money, simply as a comuter (not to exceed 70 mph) but thats because they are a sporty economy car. not a SPORTS car, but a SPORTY car, like the cavaleir,probe,camaro,firebird,& even some jags etc..... sporty, not sports. <BR>just my 3 cents<P>ps, no flaming please, fieros catch fire too easy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>surgeon generals warning: all of the above statements are opinions, not to be taken as fact. this will not hold up in a court of law, or with insurance companies. please do not read while opperating heavy machinery. flaming may result in injury. if you are pregnant and a rice lover, reading this may cause a miscariage or deformities.<BR>anything else??<P><BR>oh yeah.... dont do drugs <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000030||Nashco||11-06-2001||01:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackDragon:<BR><B>there is no replacement for displacement.<P>oh yeah.... dont do drugs </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So....CART and IRL motors are just sissy motors, huh??? LOL<P>I think that statement was true when cars first started being raced, to an extent, but since the mid to late 70's, that statement is fading out fast.  Especially with turbo technology, and even multi-valve per cylinder naturally aspirated designs, are showing this is no longer true.  Nowadays, saying displacement is best is  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">!<P>No flames intended whatsoever...if you take it that way, sorry.  I don't flame, because that would make me a flamer <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  This is all just a fun conversation.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>||||reg||1
Z||000031||BlackDragon||11-06-2001||01:42 AM||||i know the displacement thing is going out of style fast, and i didn't take it as a flame. however my veiw is that you can take all that nos, and all those turbos, and all that technology and put it on a bigger engine, and once again, there is no replacement for displacement. <BR>they are doing incredible things with little engines these days, i do not deny it. personaly my favorite engine in the world is a wankle rotary engine, because of how advanced it is, and how it works, but you can only get so much out of a little engine.<BR><P>------------------<BR>riced civics suck||||reg||1
Z||000032||Nashco||11-06-2001||01:52 AM||||Wow, this is going off topic...but I don't care <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>I agree, you can add forced induction to a bigger engine just the same as with a small enging...BUT, are we assuming packaging doesn't matter?  How many of us can fit a Big motor AND a turbo, etc?  In automotive racing, getting the maximum horsepower and torque lbs per engine pound is key.  If a twin turbo rotary motor (bad ass motors, I agree) can make the same power as a 454, what reason do we have not to go with the turbo motor?  If you can get the same power out of a smaller motor, that shouldn't be discounted.<P>It's not like turbochargin is illegal!  LOL...nobody will call you a cheater if you make more power than them with a smaller engine.  When downdraft and sidedraft carburetors became standard, did those using updraft carburetors say, "Oh, no fair, I can just put on a bigger up draft carburetor"....no...not even.<P>There's nothing wrong with technology, it's the flavor of our lives...er...something.  If we can do it with less, why not?  Yes, you can get flour by growing wheat and harvesting it yourself....but isn't buying a bag of it so much nicer?  Technology rules...utilize it.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>*If you don't like my analogies..well....uh.. you're a poopy head!*||||reg||1
Z||000033||Monkeyman||11-06-2001||05:34 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000034||Kasdan||11-06-2001||07:24 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B><P>People like to trash-talk Civics. They're a freaking <I>economy</I> car. They do what they were designed to do, and they do it well.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Umm, what the crap fo you think our cars are?  Theres probably a reason Pontiac marketed the 2m4 (and probably the V6's) as ECONOMY COMMUTERS.  Stop being so hypocritical about FWD cars, our cars have just as many problems, if not less, then a Del Sol.  I see many more Del Sol's on the Road, and i was looking at a Del Sol forum, and trust me, they had more members and a whole lot less problems on the tech board.||||reg||1
Z||000035||delSol97||11-06-2001||01:31 PM||||Multiple comments:<P>For some of the posters on here, the Fiero as we all know, has one of the worst stigma's out there.  Its reputation is below poor in the general public's mind.  We know its different, but most people call Fiero's deathtraps, firebombs, etc.   So for some Fiero people to make comments about "delSol's" based on what they've "heard" is downright funny.<P><BR>Sorry, I don't follow "Solo" competition.  Now you guys are gonna force me to go pull out results now aren't you?<P><BR>Displacement:<P>Considering most 4cyl import engines now are putting out more HP now than '80s era Chevy 350's.  I'm one to believe that, yes, indeed, there is a replacement for displacement.<P>On top of that, they're getting triple the gas mileage.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000036||Formula||11-06-2001||02:12 PM||||honda doesnt make fast cars?<P>prelude<BR>s2000<P>lets not even go into acura....||||reg||1
Z||000037||BN Boomer||11-06-2001||02:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by delSol97:<BR><B><BR>Displacement:<P>Considering most 4cyl import engines now are putting out more HP now than '80s era Chevy 350's.  I'm one to believe that, yes, indeed, there is a replacement for displacement.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wow, talk about comparing apples and oranges. Chevy 350s are now putting out more HP than 80's era Chevy 350s, too. And will absolutlely KILL any 4 banger in the torque department (you know, that stuff that actually does the work). It's called automotive evolution. How about putting your new import 4 banger in ANY car that Chevrolet put a 350 into during the 80s and seeing how well it performs or how long it lasts? What's yer point? <P>Anything you can do to a little 4 banger you can do to a large V-8, too, and get equally impressive gains in performance. <P>And as long as we are this far of topic, I would like to see you apply your "yes, indeed, there is a replacement for displacement" logic to another area of automotive performance: towing. Let's see how that super-twin turbo-charged DOHC 24 valve 4 bangin' mega mill does in a 3/4 or 1 ton truck. Oh yeah, that darn torque thing again. Must be why 4 bangers absolutely dominate drag racing, right?||||reg||1
Z||000038||Spektrum-87GT||11-06-2001||07:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Kasdan:<BR><B> Umm, what the crap fo you think our cars are?  Theres probably a reason Pontiac marketed the 2m4 (and probably the V6's) as ECONOMY COMMUTERS.  Stop being so hypocritical about FWD cars, our cars have just as many problems, if not less, then a Del Sol.  I see many more Del Sol's on the Road, and i was looking at a Del Sol forum, and trust me, they had more members and a whole lot less problems on the tech board.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>say what you want about the 2m4 being a economy commuter, the gt definitly wasnt!! they started at around 13k back in 87!!! thats not exactly economy for 15 years ago, neither is the gas mileage. i've driven four banger fieros, all i have to say is that you cant compare them with a 2m6/gt/formula, its a completely different ride. i agree that fieros have their fair share of problems, what car doesnt?||||reg||1
Z||000039||BlackDragon||11-07-2001||02:56 PM||||hey, del sol guy, this is a fiero loving forum. we love fiero's, that is why we are here. i havent heard one good thing from you about the fiero. maybe im wrong, but i dont think you belong.<BR>im not saying little engines suck. technology is great, but i agree with boomer, and nashco. if a little engine will suit your purpose, with a whole bunch of bolt ons, thats great, use the small engine. however, there are some aplications where a 4cyl would be a joke. would you buy a viper for $70,000.00 with a 4cyl that has enough turbo to give it 400 hp?? or would you go for the v10 option for the same price??? nuf said. a 4cyl is great in a little car. or if you want economy, but if you can fit a v8, JUST DO IT. this is completely off topic, but when i started the thread, i knew it would be  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> i figured this would be a controversial subject, but thats ok, i think we can all keep our cool and act like adults. <P>hhmmmm, i could put more, but im trying not to start a realy big war here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> have a nice day  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
